.16,133.2,126.45,130.01,52673000],[131.15,132.79,129.05,131.54,39285100]],"about":{"what":"Apple Inc. (AAPL). This chart runs from Sep 20, 2007 to Jan 29, 2008.","setup":"The stock rose about 73% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $192.68 and pulling back 22% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Dec 7, 2007 it closed at $194.30, its first close above the base high of $192.73. Volume that day was 38.1M shares, 1.07x the prior 10-day average of 35.7M. It didn't hold. By Dec 13, 2007 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $131.54.","lesson":"This is an example of a false breakout. Volume on the breakout day was light, and that tell was visible before the move fell apart. Cutting it early was a good read."}}